/-! ## Computable witnesses

`computableWitness` peels `main` the way `mainCost` does, keyed on the circuit
former (`cw_peel`, `ComputableWitness.lean`): the eleven witness-IR sites go to
the agreement lemmas of `IRAgree`, every gadget child to its own
`computableWitnesses` through `CW.flat_assertion` / `CW.flat_general`, and the
`Circuit.map` of `Step` through `CW.map_iff`.  The two local tactics discharge a
child's "the child's input is determined below the offset" obligation: every
component is either a cell of an earlier witness block (closed by the agreement
hypothesis and `omega` on the offset arithmetic), a projection of `main`'s own
input, or one of the `sumOver` sums over the per-position signals.

The arithmetic is kept inside `omega`'s fragment by rewriting every child's
`localLength` to its numeral during the peel, so the offsets are linear in `n`
and the loop index; the numerals are the `allocations` halves of the `Count`s in
`Cost.lean` (e.g. `stepCost = ⟨1269, _⟩`). -/
section ComputableWitnessPeel

